10
00:40:28,571 --> 00:40:34,571
"Don't Look Back in Anger" is a song by English rock band Oasis, released on 19 February 1996 by Creation
Records as the fifth single from their second studio album, (What's the Story) Morning Glory?

11
00:44:31,428 --> 00:44:37,428
"Don't Look Back in Anger" was written by the lead guitarist and chief
songwriter, Noel Gallagher, and produced by Gallagher and Owen Morris.

12
00:48:34,285 --> 00:48:40,285
It was the first Oasis single with lead vocals by Noel, who had previously
only sung lead on B-sides, instead of his brother, Liam.

13
00:52:37,142 --> 00:52:43,142
Noel later sang lead vocals on six other singles.

14
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
The single was the second Oasis song to reach number one on the UK singles
chart, and it was certified seven times platinum in the UK.

15
01:00:42,857 --> 01:00:48,857
The music video was directed by Nigel Dick, featuring Oasis
performing at a mansion with a large group of women.

16
01:04:45,714 --> 01:04:51,714
Critically, the song received positive reviews.

17
01:08:48,571 --> 01:08:54,571
It is one of Oasis's signature songs and has been
played at almost every live show.

18
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
In later decades, it has been included in retrospective rankings of best songs, and
has been described as an "anthem" by critics in various contexts.

19
01:16:54,285 --> 01:17:00,285
The film explores themes of trauma, death of father, public murder, karma.

20
01:20:57,142 --> 01:21:03,142
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
